#{[17592186247187 :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ then the equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}[A\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -2 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -2 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & k-2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-10\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} &=1 \\\\ -2{x}_{2} &=-4 \\\\ 0 &=k-10.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k-10,$ which means that $k=10.$"] [17592186247188 :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by $L=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}7k-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(L).$"] [17592186247188 :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\text{Col}(L),$ then the equation $L\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[L\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}[L\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}8 & -1 & 7k-1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & \\leftrightarrow {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -1 & 7k-1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 8 & -1 & 7k-1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-8{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 7k-25\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\left(-\\frac{1}{4}\\right){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 7k-25\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+9{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7k-7\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=3 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=2 \\\\ 0 &=7k-7.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=7k-7,$ which means that $k=1.$"] [17592186247190 :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ k \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(A).$"] [17592186247190 :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ then the equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}[A\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-5 & 1 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & \\leftrightarrow {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ -5 & 1 & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ 0 & 6 & 42\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ 0 & 0 & 42+2k\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=10 \\\\ -3{x}_{2} &=k \\\\ 0 &=42+2k.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=42+2k,$ which means that $k=-21.$"] [17592186247191 :question/problem "The matrix $C$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ are given below.\nDetermine if $\\mathbf{b}\\in \\text{Col}(C).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$, where ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers such that $\\mathbf{b}={x}_{1}{\\mathbf{c}}_{\\mathbf{1}}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{c}}_{\\mathbf{2}}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{c}}_{\\mathbf{3}},$ and ${\\mathbf{c}}_{1}$, ${\\mathbf{c}}_{2}$, and ${\\mathbf{c}}_{\\mathbf{3}}$ are the respective columns of $C.$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{2em}\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ -12 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [17592186247191 :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\text{Col}(C),$ we need to check if the equation $C\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[C\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}[C\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & -12 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -14\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 10\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=-8 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=-12 \\\\ 5{x}_{3} &=10.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting it into the second equation gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}-(2) & =-12 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, from the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =-8-3{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} \\\\  & =-8-3(-5)-3(2) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $C\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent, which implies that $\\mathbf{b}\\in \\text{Col}(C).$ \n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $\\mathbf{b}$ as a linear combination of ${\\mathbf{c}}_{1},$ ${\\mathbf{c}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{c}}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ -12 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}}_{\\mathbf{b}}=1\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{{\\mathbf{c}}_{1}}+(-5)\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{{\\mathbf{c}}_{2}}+2\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{{\\mathbf{c}}_{3}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=1\\cdot (-5)\\cdot 2=-10.$"] [17592186247192 :question/problem "The matrix $M$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ are given below.\nDetermine if $\\mathbf{b}\\in \\text{Col}(M).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$, where ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers such that $\\mathbf{b}={x}_{1}{\\mathbf{m}}_{\\mathbf{1}}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{m}}_{\\mathbf{2}}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{m}}_{\\mathbf{3}},$ and ${\\mathbf{m}}_{1}$, ${\\mathbf{m}}_{2}$, and ${\\mathbf{m}}_{\\mathbf{3}}$ are the respective columns of $M.$\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{2em}\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [17592186247192 :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\text{Col}(M),$ we need to check if the equation $M\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[M\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}[M\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 & -24 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & \\leftrightarrow {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 & -24\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 8\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=9 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=8 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFinally, from the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+(8) & =9 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $M\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent, which implies that $\\mathbf{b}\\in \\text{Col}(M).$ \n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $\\mathbf{b}$ as a linear combination of ${\\mathbf{m}}_{1},$ ${\\mathbf{m}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{m}}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}}_{\\mathbf{b}}=1\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{{\\mathbf{m}}_{1}}+8\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{{\\mathbf{m}}_{2}}+2\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{{\\mathbf{m}}_{3}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=1\\cdot 8\\cdot 2=16.$"] [17592186247198 :question/problem "The matrix $E$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ are given below.\nDetermine if $\\mathbf{b}\\in \\text{Col}(E).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{4}$, where ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, ${x}_{3}$, and ${x}_{4}$ are real numbers such that $\\mathbf{b}={x}_{1}{\\mathbf{e}}_{\\mathbf{1}}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{e}}_{\\mathbf{2}}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{e}}_{\\mathbf{3}}+{x}_{4}{\\mathbf{e}}_{\\mathbf{4}},$ and ${\\mathbf{e}}_{1}$, ${\\mathbf{e}}_{2}$, ${\\mathbf{e}}_{3}$, and ${\\mathbf{e}}_{4}$ are respective columns of $E.$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -15 & 0 & 20 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{2em}\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [17592186247198 :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\text{Col}(E),$ we need to check if the equation $E\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[E\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}[E\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -3 & 0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -15 & 0 & 20 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 & -1 & 6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -3 & 0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 & -1 & 6\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+4{x}_{4} &=-2 \\\\ 0 &=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}+7{x}_{3}-{x}_{4} &=6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get a false statement $0=2.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $\\mathbf{b}\\notin \\text{Col}(E).$"] [17592186247199 :question/problem "The matrix $M$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ are given below.\nDetermine if $\\mathbf{b}\\in \\text{Col}(M).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{4}$, where ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, ${x}_{3}$, and ${x}_{4}$ are real numbers such that $\\mathbf{b}={x}_{1}{\\mathbf{m}}_{\\mathbf{1}}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{m}}_{\\mathbf{2}}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{m}}_{\\mathbf{3}}+{x}_{4}{\\mathbf{m}}_{\\mathbf{4}},$ and ${\\mathbf{m}}_{1}$, ${\\mathbf{m}}_{2}$, ${\\mathbf{m}}_{3}$, and ${\\mathbf{m}}_{4}$ are respective columns of $M.$\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -3 & 6 & -12\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{2em}\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [17592186247199 :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\text{Col}(M),$ we need to check if the equation $M\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[M\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}[M\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -3 & 6 & -12 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -8\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}+4{x}_{4} &=-3 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-{x}_{4} &=1 \\\\ 0 &=-8.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get a false statement $0=-8.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $\\mathbf{b}\\notin \\text{Col}(M).$"] [17592186317403 :question/problem "The matrix $D$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ are given below.\nDetermine if $\\mathbf{b}\\in \\text{Col}(D).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}+{x}_{4}$, where ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, ${x}_{3}$, and ${x}_{4}$ are real numbers such that $\\mathbf{b}={x}_{1}{\\mathbf{d}}_{\\mathbf{1}}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{d}}_{\\mathbf{2}}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{d}}_{\\mathbf{3}}+{x}_{4}{\\mathbf{d}}_{\\mathbf{4}},$ and ${\\mathbf{d}}_{1}$, ${\\mathbf{d}}_{2}$, ${\\mathbf{d}}_{3}$, and ${\\mathbf{d}}_{4}$ are respective columns of $D.$\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{2em}\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [17592186317403 :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\text{Col}(D),$ we need to check if the equation $D\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[D\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}[D\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & 4 & 7 & 11 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 6 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & -1 & 7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & 4 & 7 & 11 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & -1 & 7\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}+7{x}_{4} &=11 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}-{x}_{4} &=-2 \\\\ 0 &=9 \\\\ {x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}-{x}_{4} &=7.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get a false statement $0=9.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $\\mathbf{b}\\notin \\text{Col}(D).$"] [17592186317416 :question/problem "The matrix $E$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ are given below.\nDetermine if $\\mathbf{b}\\in \\text{Col}(E).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{4}$, where ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, ${x}_{3}$, and ${x}_{4}$ are real numbers such that $\\mathbf{b}={x}_{1}{\\mathbf{e}}_{\\mathbf{1}}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{e}}_{\\mathbf{2}}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{e}}_{\\mathbf{3}}+{x}_{4}{\\mathbf{e}}_{\\mathbf{4}},$ and ${\\mathbf{e}}_{1}$, ${\\mathbf{e}}_{2}$, ${\\mathbf{e}}_{3}$, and ${\\mathbf{e}}_{4}$ are respective columns of $E.$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 16 & -4 & 10 & 2 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{2em}\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [17592186317416 :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\text{Col}(E),$ we need to check if the equation $E\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[E\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}[E\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}8 & -2 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 16 & -4 & 10 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}8 & -2 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}8{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}+{x}_{4} &=4 \\\\ 0 &=-9 \\\\ 11{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}-{x}_{4} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get a false statement $0=-9.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $\\mathbf{b}\\notin \\text{Col}(E).$"] [17592186317417 :question/problem "The matrix $F$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ are given below. Determine if $\\mathbf{b}\\in \\text{Col}(F).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $\\mathbf{b}={x}_{1}{\\mathbf{f}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{f}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{f}}_{1},$  ${\\mathbf{f}}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $F.$\n\n$$\nF=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{2em}\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [17592186317417 :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\text{Col}(F),$ we need to check if the equation $F\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[F\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}[F\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -14\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} &=5 \\\\ 7{x}_{2} &=-14.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ Substituting into the first equation gives  ${x}_{1}=1.$ \n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $F\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent, which implies that $\\mathbf{b}\\in \\text{Col}(F).$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $\\mathbf{b}$ as a linear combination of ${\\mathbf{f}}_{1}$ and ${\\mathbf{f}}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{\\mathbf{b}}=1\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}}_{{\\mathbf{f}}_{\\mathbf{1}}}+(-2)\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{{\\mathbf{f}}_{\\mathbf{2}}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=1\\cdot (-2)=-2.$"] [17592186323698 :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 4 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(A).$"] [17592186323698 :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ then the equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}[A\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -7 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 5 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & \\leftrightarrow {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -7 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 5 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 17 & k-12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-17){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+5\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2} &=4 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=-1 \\\\ 0 &=k+5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k+5,$ which means that $k=-5.$"] [17592186342180 :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ are given below. Determine if $\\mathbf{b}\\in \\text{Col}(A).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $\\mathbf{b}={x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},$ ${\\mathbf{a}}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $A.$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{2em}\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [17592186342180 :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ we need to check if the equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}[A\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=2 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=5 \\\\ 0 &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get the false statement $0=1.$ \n\nTherefore, the system is inconsistent, which implies that $\\mathbf{b}\\notin \\text{Col}(A).$"] [17592186342184 :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by $B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{bmatrix}.$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ k-3\\end{bmatrix}$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(B).$"] [17592186342184 :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\text{Col}(B),$ then the equation $B\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[B\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}[B\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 7 & k-3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 7 & k-3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k+2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=-1 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=-1 \\\\ 0 &=k-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k-1,$ which means that $k=1.$"] [17592186342185 :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by $L=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}k-11 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(L).$"] [17592186342185 :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\text{Col}(L),$ then the equation $L\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[L\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}[L\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & 1 & k-11 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -10 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & \\leftrightarrow {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -10 \\\\ 3 & 1 & k-11\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 3 & 1 & k-11\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 4 & k+4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-16\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=5 \\\\ 2{x}_{2} &=10 \\\\ 0 &=k-16.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k-16,$ which means that $k=16.$"] [17592186342186 :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by $M=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2k+10\\end{bmatrix}$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(M).$"] [17592186342186 :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\text{Col}(M),$ then the equation $M\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[M\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}[M\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{b}] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 3 & 2k+10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & \\leftrightarrow {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 3 & 2k+10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 3 & 2k+10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-6){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 15 & 2k+10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-5){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2k-10\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{2} &=4 \\\\ 0 &=2k-10.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=2k-10,$ which means that $k=5.$"] [17592186342189 :question/problem "The matrix $M$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ are given below.\nDetermine if $\\mathbf{b}\\in \\text{Col}(M).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$, where ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers such that $\\mathbf{b}={x}_{1}{\\mathbf{m}}_{\\mathbf{1}}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{m}}_{\\mathbf{2}}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{m}}_{\\mathbf{3}},$ and ${\\mathbf{m}}_{1}$, ${\\mathbf{m}}_{2}$, and ${\\mathbf{m}}_{\\mathbf{3}}$ are the respective columns of $M.$\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 6 & 0 & -13\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{2em}\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"]}
